%N A319558 The squarefree dual of a multiset partition has, for each vertex, one block consisting of the indices (or positions) of the blocks containing that vertex, counted without multiplicity. Then a(n) is the number of non-isomorphic multiset partitions of weight n whose squarefree dual is strict (no repeated blocks).
%C A319558 The weight of a multiset partition is the sum of sizes of its parts. Weight is generally not the same as number of vertices.
%H A319558 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A319558/b319558.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..35</a>
%e A319558 Non-isomorphic representatives of the a(1) = 1, a(2) = 3, and a(3) = 7 multiset partitions:
%e A319558 1:    {{1}}
%e A319558 2:   {{1,1}}
%e A319558     {{1},{1}}
%e A319558     {{1},{2}}
%e A319558 3:  {{1,1,1}}
%e A319558    {{1},{1,1}}
%e A319558    {{1},{2,2}}
%e A319558    {{2},{1,2}}
%e A319558   {{1},{1},{1}}
%e A319558   {{1},{2},{2}}
%e A319558   {{1},{2},{3}}
